{
  "key": "letter-166-part-01",
  "number": 166,
  "generationId": "01a1e8e3-b68f-7d2b-81f8-e24cad249b8d",
  "voice": "Views",
  "speed": 0.9,
  "clips": [
    {
      "index": 0,
      "text": "Love.",
      "path": "audio/1971-166/01.mp3",
      "start": 0.0,
      "end": 0.573447
    },
    {
      "index": 1,
      "text": "Always see what is - the facts.",
      "path": "audio/1971-166/02.mp3",
      "start": 1.730385,
      "end": 4.484694
    },
    {
      "index": 2,
      "text": "That which is.",
      "path": "audio/1971-166/03.mp3",
      "start": 5.6170979999999995,
      "end": 6.4825170000000005
    },
    {
      "index": 3,
      "text": "Do not project anything, do not interpret, do not impose any meaning: that is, do not allow your mind to interfere, and you will begin to encounter reality.",
      "path": "audio/1971-166/04.mp3",
      "start": 7.602041,
      "end": 17.01941
    },
    {
      "index": 4,
      "text": "Otherwise everyone lives in his own world of dreaming.",
      "path": "audio/1971-166/05.mp3",
      "start": 18.201110999999997,
      "end": 21.259796
    },
    {
      "index": 5,
      "text": "And meditation is the coming out of these worlds, these dreaming patterns.",
      "path": "audio/1971-166/06.mp3",
      "start": 22.897098,
      "end": 27.608889
    },
    {
      "index": 6,
      "text": "A philosopher stopped Mulla Nasrudin on the street.",
      "path": "audio/1971-166/07.mp3",
      "start": 29.13263,
      "end": 32.35585
    },
    {
      "index": 7,
      "text": "In order to test whether the Mulla was sensitive to philosophical knowledge he made a sign, pointing at the sky.",
      "path": "audio/1971-166/08.mp3",
      "start": 33.871247000000004,
      "end": 40.273559999999996
    },
    {
      "index": 8,
      "text": "The philosopher meant: There is only one truth, which covers all.",
      "path": "audio/1971-166/09.mp3",
      "start": 41.849819000000004,
      "end": 46.994014
    },
    {
      "index": 9,
      "text": "Nasrudin's companion, an ordinary man, thought: The philosopher is mad.",
      "path": "audio/1971-166/10.mp3",
      "start": 48.574921,
      "end": 55.12
    }
  ]
}
